**The one finding (GAP-1)**

The transport rejects only CR and NUL, so the eight universal-newline characters (VT, FF, FS, GS, RS, NEL, LS, PS) pass inside a content line. An LF-only parser sees 14 paths, but a Python `splitlines()` parser sees 15. The producer's own independent test parser has this blind spot. The real apply_patch tool's line semantics were not examined. None of the 22 inputs contains those bytes, so the historical exercise is unaffected. The cheap fix is to reject those eight characters in `make_patch`; I did not apply it.

